<title>UK: Abbey disappointed by mortgage tax change.</title>
<headline>Abbey disappointed by mortgage tax change.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's second largest mortgage lender Abbey National Plc said on Wednesday it was disappointed by the Labour government's decision to cut mortgage interest tax relief (MIRAS) to 10 percent from 15 percent, as of April 1998.</p>
<p>&quot;We are disappointed that the typical homeowner will face an extra 10 pound charge from next April,&quot; an Abbey National spokesperson told Reuters. Chancellor of the Exchequer announced the change in his first budget.</p>
</text>
